  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-3 configs all use scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer aggregation. Within this family, vit_l+weighted (config_041, acc=0.7250) is best on accuracy, but resnet50+weighted (config_015, acc=0.7131) achieves the best F1 (0.6945), suggesting resnet50 captures complementary discriminative information. The vit_l+concat variant (config_025, acc=0.7207) is only marginally below weighted. Question: Does resnet50+concat (config_049) synergize—combining resnet50's stronger F1 signal with concat's feature-preserving fusion—to match or exceed 0.7250? This completes the 2×2 grid {vit_l, resnet50}×{weighted, concat} for the best architecture, resolving the last uncertainty in the top-performing family. Why this experiment: With 2 runs remaining, this is the highest-information test within the proven best architecture; if it underperforms, we confirm config_041 as the winner and can spend remaining budget on a cheap confirmation or a long-shot alternative. Expected cost: ~5.5 GPU hours (transformer aggregation + resnet50, comparable to config_015's 6.22 but concat fusion is slightly cheaper than weighted), making it a moderate-cost experiment relative to the budget already spent (27.22 GPU hrs)."
}

